  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve():\n    # Analyze the given examples to determine the rule\n    # It appears that the rule is to take the sub-grids with different numbers \n    # and move their borders one cell towards the center\n\n    def apply_rule(grid):\n        rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n        output_grid = [[cell for cell in row] for row in grid]\n        \n        for num in set(num for row in grid for num in row):\n            if num == grid[0][0]:\n                continue\n\n            top, bottom, left, right = float('inf'), float('-inf'), float('inf'), float('-inf')\n            for i in range(rows):\n                for j in range(cols):\n                    if grid[i][j] == num:\n                        top, bottom = min(top, i), max(bottom, i)\n                        left, right = min(left, j), max(right, j)\n\n            for i in range(rows):\n                for j in range(cols):\n                    if (i >= top and i <= bottom and j >= left and j <= right and \n                        not (i > top and i < bottom and j > left and j < right)):\n                        output_grid[i][j] = num\n                    elif (i == top or i == bottom or j == left or j == right):\n                        output_grid[i][j] = grid[i][j]\n\n        return output_grid\n\n    test_input = [\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 1, 8, 8, 1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 1, 1, 1, 1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 1, 1, 1, 1, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 2, 2, 2, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 2, 2, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 2, 2, 2, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 4, 4, 4, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 4, 8, 4, 8, 8, 8, 8],\n        [8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8]\n    ]\n\n    output_grid = apply_rule(test_input)\n    return output_grid\n\noutput = solve()\nprint(output)\n```",
